      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "Just to see if I understood correctly, the reason why these strings are being suggested to be split is so on some cases the translations capitalized the first word, and in other cases the capitalization is on the second word?\n\nIs there a grammatical or other reference rule that goes against not using a consistent capitalization method for all types? Or in other words, if strings were capitalized the same way in all places and differenced from each other by their UI styling (title vs in-line text) just like English does, is there something that readers in non-romance languages miss from their meaning?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
