      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{628d00a6b624bb0b622328ef|full_name} No, It Just Looks Ugly Because No One Types In Russian In This Camel Case, Even In Titles. Its Not Grammatical Rule. More Like Formatting And Stylistic Code. Meaning Is Not Lost.\n\nIf it's not possible to keep variants of strings, we'll probably just fall back to normal (First character only) casing in titles too. For consistency, everywhere. But I afraid some titles might share strings with buttons too, so... This means then we have to make buttons normal casing for consistency too. 🤔\n\nAnd I can't say for other languages.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
