      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a9fe9983955314156acc4f7|full_name} Got it, thanks for the examples! I'm glad its mainly a formatting discussion rather than a meaning one.\n\nWhen it comes to styling I know English uses \"**T**itle **C**ase\" but this may seem odd in other languages, Spanish for example uses \"**S**entence case\" which only caps the first letter of the first sentence and this is perfectly fine for all elements (buttons, headers, in-line, etc.) with the exception of acronyms (like VRC) and names. Does that work for Russian as well? I'm curious about other votes on this post too in case it applies to their language as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
